Carafe: with BridgeReturn, the WoW64 system-call and unix-call bridge leaves as a return. The guest reaches the bridge
through a call, and the bridge goes on at the return address that call left on the stack, so the call-return stack
kept the call's entry: every later return of the outer frames then popped the entry of the frame below it and missed.
The exit now looks at the top of the call-return stack and, when it holds the return address, pops it and returns to
its host code; otherwise it leaves the stack alone and takes the lookup as before. Off by default.
MIT, as the files it changes.

